      "title": "Academic Dean’s Office",
      "description": "Academic Dean's Office - Goshen College Skip to Main Content Language Toggle Search Toggle Search our site Search Menu Menu Toggle Apply Get Info Visit Give New Students Parents & Families Alumni Community Academics Menu Toggle Undergraduate Programs Graduate and Licensure Programs Honors Program Global Engagement Academic Dean’s Office Registrar’s Office Admissions and Aid Menu Toggle Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Licensure Admissions Financial Aid Scholarships Net Price Calculator Visit Athletics Menu Toggle Recruiting Maple Leaf Athletic Club Watch Live Give to MLAC Student Life Menu Toggle Campus Housing Dining Clubs and Extracurriculars Campus Ministries Campus Safety Center for Health & Wellness About Menu Toggle Who We Are News and Events Facilities and Centers Employment Give to Goshen College Contact Us and Campus Directory Academics Academics Undergraduate Programs Menu Toggle Majors and Minors Honors Program Experiential Learning Graduate and Licensure Programs Menu Toggle Master of Arts in Teaching Master of Arts in Environmental Education Master of Business Administration Master of Science in Nursing Master of Social Work Doctor of Nursing Practice Transition to Teaching Licensure English Learners Licensure Global Engagement Menu Toggle Detroit India London, U.K. Northern Ireland On Campus Puerto Rico Tanzania U.S. South: Freedom Summer Academic Dean’s Office Menu Toggle Faculty Career Network Menu Toggle Employer Resources Jobs & Internships Board Registrar’s Office Academic Dean’s Office Meet our Faculty Academic Calendar Registrar's Office The Academic Dean’s office provides the leadership, resources and services to nurture faculty excellence in their field and in the classroom. Goshen College academics equips students with the intellectual skills, spiritual and ethical commitments, and global understanding that prepare them for lives of meaning and service in local and global communities. With a commitment to the highest standards of intellectual integrity Goshen College faculty create an inclusive, student-centered learning environment that nurtures curiosity and integrity, collaboration and community engagement, rigor and joy. Academic Programs and Student Success The Dean’s Office coordinates the academic services that help you thrive at Goshen College. These include the Registrar’s Office, the Academic Success Center, the Good Library, Career Networks, and orientation and retention programs. We also oversee the GC Core curriculum, global engagement opportunities, adult and graduate programs, and the Music Center — ensuring that every student has access to resources for meaningful, equitable success. Academic Governance and Policy The Dean’s Office provides leadership for academic governance. Regular committees and forums guide decision-making and academic policy across divisions, including the Professional School, Science and Nursing, and Humanities and Social Sciences. Teaching and Curriculum Vice President for Academic Affairs and Academic Dean, Ann Vendrely, oversees teaching and curriculum across all programs. Goshen offers undergraduate and graduate learning on campus, online, and at distinctive locations — the Merry Lea Environmental Learning Center in Wolf Lake, Indiana, and the J.N. Roth Marine Biology Station in Layton, Florida. Research and Professional Development Scholarship and innovation are central to the Goshen experience. Through the Mininger Center, faculty receive support for research, mentoring, and teaching development. Students gain their own opportunities for discovery through the Maple & Hickory Scholars summer research program and the Annual Academic Symposium, where excellence across disciplines is celebrated. Explore our Faculty Publications Academic Leadership Dr. Ann M. Vendrely Vice President for Academic Affairs and Academic Dean; Professor of Kinesiology Dr. Jan Kauffman Associate Dean Student Success Dr. Suzanne Ehst Associate Academic Dean Solidia Brown Assistant to Academic Programs Dr. Justin Heinzekehr Director of Institutional Research and Assessment; Assistant Professor of Bible and Religion Fritz Hartman Director of Library Michelle Horning Professor of Accounting, Program Director, 2026–27 Faculty Chair Previous Next Academics Menu Toggle Undergraduate Programs Graduate and Licensure Programs Honors Program Global Engagement Academic Dean’s Office Registrar’s Office Admissions and Aid Menu Toggle Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Licensure Admissions Financial Aid Scholarships Net Price Calculator Visit Athletics Menu Toggle Recruiting Maple Leaf Athletic Club Watch Live Give to MLAC Student Life Menu Toggle Campus Housing Dining Clubs and Extracurriculars Campus Ministries Campus Safety Center for Health & Wellness About Menu Toggle Who We Are News and Events Facilities and Centers Employment Give to Goshen College Contact Us and Campus Directory Address 1700 South Main Street Goshen, IN 46526 Get directions Phone Directory News & Events Employment Give Athletics New Students MyGC Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Title IX Website Feedback Form © 2026\t\tGoshen College Alert JavaScript is disabled This site requires JavaScript to function properly. We use cookies Our site uses cookies to enhance your site experience in accordance with our privacy policy . By continuing to use our site, you agree to our use of cookies. OK We use cookies Our site uses cookies to enhance your site experience in accordance with our privacy policy . By continuing to use our site, you agree to our use of cookies. Google reCAPTCHA response"
