nt Martin Saint Pierre and Miquelon Saint Vincent and the Grenadines Samoa San Marino Sao Tome and Principe Saudi Arabia Senegal Serbia Seychelles Sierra Leone Singapore Sint Maarten Slovakia Slovenia Solomon Islands Somalia South Africa South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands South Sudan Spain Sri Lanka Sudan Suriname Svalbard and Jan Mayen Sweden Switzerland Syria Arab Republic Taiwan Tajikistan Tanzania, the United Republic of Thailand Timor-Leste Togo Tokelau Tonga Trinidad and Tobago Tunisia Türkiye Turkmenistan Turks and Caicos Islands Tuvalu Uganda Ukraine United Arab Emirates United Kingdom United States Uruguay US Minor Outlying Islands Uzbekistan Vanuatu Venezuela Viet Nam Virgin Islands, British Virgin Islands, U.S. Wallis and Futuna Western Sahara Yemen Zambia Zimbabwe Country My Permanent Address is (Required) the same as Current Address different from Current Address What position are you applying for? (Required) How did you hear of this position? (Required) Newspaper Friend/Relative Employment Agency Website Other Have you been previously employed at Goshen College? (Required) Yes No Are you eligible to work in the U.S.? (Proof of citizenship or immigration status will be required upon employment.) (Required) Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B, O-1, etc.)? Yes No Have you ever been convicted of a felony? (Required) Yes No (A conviction does not automatically constitute a rejection of employment.) Professional Qualifications Upload Documents (Required) Max. file size: 50 MB. Attach resume, cover letter and other supporting documents here. You may also send attachments separately to [email protected] . Reflections on GC's vision, mission, and core values Goshen College is rooted in the way of Jesus and is affiliated with Mennonite Church USA, a historic Anabaptist peace church. Our expression of faith is not a simple matter of words spoken at appointed times, but of word and deed fitted into the context of the routine of daily life and work. In a community where the intellect is nurtured, it is also important to develop a reflective faith which can be expressed in campus discussion. A respect and appreciation of the Anabaptist-Mennonite faith perspective and practices, and a commitment to the mission, vision, core values and community standards of Goshen College, are important for all teaching and administrative faculty members. Please read the mission, vision and values of the college. Reflect on the compatibility of these statements with your sense of vocation and, if applying for a teaching position, your philosophy of education including the integration of faith and learning. (Required) The mission of the college reflects an Anabaptist-Mennonite understanding of Christian faith. Give a brief statement of your personal faith journey and a reflection on how you align with and are committed to the college’s mission, vision and core values. (Required) The mission of the college reflects an Anabaptist-Mennonite understanding of Christian faith. Give a brief statement of your personal faith journey and a reflection on how you align with and are committed to the college’s mission, vision and core values. Please read the mission, vision and values of the college. Are you willing to support the vision, mission, and core values of Goshen College? (Required) This field is hidden when viewing the form Do you regularly attend a church? Yes No Other This field is hidden when viewing the form Other This field is hidden when viewing the form Denomination This field is hidden when viewing the form Congregation This field is hidden when viewing the form Place This field is hidden when viewing the form Pastor's Name and Address Please list service/volunteer assignments and involvement in church and/or community (Required) Safety If you are interested, the Campus Safety and Fire Report is available at www.goshen.edu/safety/annual-campus-safety-report/. Affirmative Action Survey (optional) We consider all applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or any legally protected status. As a church-owned institution, Goshen College exercises its legal right to seek employees who support the mission and values of the college. Gender Male Female Other This field is hidden when viewing the form Other Check all that apply African-American, Non-Hispanic American Indian or Alaskan Native Asian or Pacific Islander Hispanic White, Non-Hispanic Person with a disability Vietnam Era Veteran African-American, Non-Hispanic - A U.S. citizen having origins in any of the Black racial groups of Africa. American Indian or Alaskan Native - A U.S. citizen having origins in any of the original people of North America and who maintains identification through tribal affiliation or community recognition. Asian or Pacific Islander - A U.S. citizen having origins in any of the original peoples of the Far East, Southeast Asia, the Indian Subcontinent or the Pacific Islands. This area includes, for example, China, Japan, Korea, the Philippine Islands and Samoa. Hispanic - A U.S. citizen of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Cuban, Central or South American or other Spanish culture or origin, regardless of race. White, Non-Hispanic - A U.S. citizen having origins in any of the original peoples of Europe, North Africa or the Middle East. Handicapped - “Handicapped” means any person who (1) has a physical or mental impairment which substantially limits one or more major life activities, (2) has a record of such impairment, or (3) is regarded as having such an impairment. Vietnam Era Veteran - Any veteran of the armed services who between Aug. 5, 1964, and May 7, 1975, served on active duty for at least 181 consecutive days or was discharged sooner because of a service-related disability. Agreement I certify that answers given herein, as well as all documents submitted as part